                <p>
                    Effective portfolio management requires organizations to look beyond
                    individual product performance and understand how products collectively
                    contribute to strategic and financial objectives.
                </p>

                <ul class="list-unstyled">
                    <li>
                        <p><i class="bi bi-check2-circle color"></i> <b>Strategic Alignment:</b> Ensure portfolio investments support the organization's overall business strategy.</p>
                    </li>
                    <li>
                        <p><i class="bi bi-check2-circle color"></i> <b>Customer Value:</b> Evaluate products according to the value they provide to target customers and markets.</p>
                    </li>
                    <li>
                        <p><i class="bi bi-check2-circle color"></i> <b>Financial Performance:</b> Consider revenue, profitability, cost, investment requirements, and future financial potential.</p>
                    </li>
                    <li>
                        <p><i class="bi bi-check2-circle color"></i> <b>Risk Management:</b> Identify and balance technical, financial, operational, and market risks across the portfolio.</p>
                    </li>
                    <li>
                        <p><i class="bi bi-check2-circle color"></i> <b>Resource Optimization:</b> Allocate people, technology, and investment to products with the strongest strategic potential.</p>
                    </li>
                    <li>
                        <p><i class="bi bi-check2-circle color"></i> <b>Market Opportunities:</b> Monitor market changes and identify opportunities for growth, innovation, and expansion.</p>
                    </li>
                    <li>
                        <p><i class="bi bi-check2-circle color"></i> <b>Continuous Evaluation:</b> Regularly review portfolio performance and adjust decisions based on measurable results.</p>
                    </li>
                </ul>
            </div>

