<section>
    <div class="container">
        <div class="row">
            <div class="col-lg-8" align="justify">
                <h3><b>Common Product Portfolio Management Challenges and How to Address Them</b></h3>

                <p>
                    Managing a portfolio of products can become complex when organizations
                    have limited resources, competing priorities, aging products, and
                    changing market conditions. A structured portfolio management approach
                    helps address these challenges.
                </p>

                <h5><b>Too Many Products and Initiatives</b></h5>
                <p>
                    Large portfolios can spread resources too thinly across multiple
                    products. Portfolio reviews help identify products that should be
                    prioritized, consolidated, improved, or discontinued.
                </p>

                <h5><b>Competing Investment Priorities</b></h5>
                <p>
                    Different products may compete for the same budget, talent, and
                    technology resources. A transparent evaluation framework helps
                    organizations allocate investment according to strategic value.
                </p>

                <h5><b>Underperforming Products</b></h5>
                <p>
                    Some products may continue receiving investment despite declining
                    customer demand or financial performance. Regular portfolio analysis
                    helps identify products that require repositioning or strategic
                    changes.
                </p>

                <h5><b>Lack of Portfolio Visibility</b></h5>
                <p>
                    Without centralized information about product performance, investment,
                    risks, and opportunities, leadership teams may struggle to make
                    informed decisions. Portfolio dashboards and structured reviews
                    improve visibility.
                </p>

                <h5><b>Changing Market Conditions</b></h5>
                <p>
                    Customer expectations, competitors, technology, and market conditions
                    can change rapidly. Portfolio strategies should be flexible enough to
                    respond to these changes.
                </p>

                <h5><b>Difficulty Balancing Innovation and Stability</b></h5>
                <p>
                    Organizations need to maintain successful existing products while
                    investing in new opportunities. Portfolio management helps create a
                    balanced approach between current performance and future growth.
                </p>
            </div>

            <div class="col-lg-4 text-center">
                @* Add the relevant portfolio challenges image here when available. *@
            </div>
