                </p>

                <h5><b>Strategic Importance</b></h5>
                <p>
                    Evaluate how strongly each product supports the organization's
                    strategic direction, market position, customer relationships, and
                    long-term objectives.
                </p>

                <h5><b>Growth Potential</b></h5>
                <p>
                    Identify products and opportunities that have the potential to expand
                    into new customer segments, markets, use cases, or revenue streams.
                </p>

                <h5><b>Risk and Complexity</b></h5>
                <p>
                    Consider technical, operational, financial, regulatory, and market
                    risks before making major portfolio investment decisions.
                </p>

                <h5><b>Portfolio Balance</b></h5>
                <p>
                    Maintain an appropriate balance between established products,
                    growth-focused initiatives, and innovative opportunities to support
                    both current performance and future development.
                </p>
